  by: agent  # b2d4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b2d4
  clock: 3  # b2d4
  nonce: b2d4  # b2d4
  message: "TAG STRIPPED as a filing-time pre-tag (queue-drain audit, 2026-08-01, dev 529e4aebe3).\n\nThe tagging discipline applies the tag AT PR MERGE TIME to a quantitative claim that exists in a\nPR description or a discussion entry. This item has pr_ref=null, an EMPTY discussion, created ==\nupdated at 2026-07-31T23:09:25Z, and states its claim conditionally in its own description:\n\"Carries a dead-code claim IF IT LANDS\". Nothing has landed. Bucket E-misapplied per the\nqueue-processing playbook, whose phase 2 says strip immediately.\n\nVERIFIED IN SOURCE before stripping (not inferred from the empty discussion):\n  - linkers/type_hierarchy.py:95 _extends_admits_dispatch still takes only\n    (language, child_kind, child_modifiers). The parent-abstract widening this item proposes is\n    not merely unimplemented, it is not expressible through that signature.\n  - NO_VIRTUAL_EXTENDS_LANGUAGES still holds all four of go/cpp/rust/csharp.\n  - tests/test_interface_dispatch_parity.py:111 still carries the cpp KNOWN_HOLES entry naming\n    this exact cause (\"asks whether the CHILD is abstract, and for a C++ abstract base the\n    abstract one is the PARENT\").\n  - The only commit touching type_hierarchy.py since this item was filed is 44cbc84610, the\n    INV-tihim member-name-separator fix, which is unrelated.\n\nWHY THE SIGNAL IS NOT LOST (the counter-argument was weighed, not waved off):\n  1. The re-tag instruction lives in the item DESCRIPTION, which survives the strip and is read\n     by whoever implements this.\n  2. There is a CI tripwire stronger than a tag: the parity suite runs strict xfails, so the PR\n     that widens the predicate cannot merge without deleting KNOWN_HOLES[\"cpp\"] in the same diff.\n     A tag can be forgotten; a red gate cannot.\n  3. INV-tihim's closure names this item as owner of the cpp cell.\nCost of keeping it: a DEEP cycle run today could return none of moved/no_move/inconclusive here,\nbecause there is no claimed movement to measure. The queue is declared the single source of truth\nfor pending validations, so an entry that can never resolve teaches the next drain session that\nthe list contains noise.\n\nRE-TAG when the fix ships with its dead-code claim."  # b2d4
