  nonce: 5f5e  # 5f5e
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES (line numbers only).\n\n- linkers/type_hierarchy.py:110 _extends_admits_dispatch(language, child_kind, child_modifiers) is\n  unchanged (the 08-01 note cited :95); :105 NO_VIRTUAL_EXTENDS_LANGUAGES still {go, cpp, rust, csharp};\n  :140 still returns is_abstract_type(child_kind, child_modifiers). The caller admitted_inheritance_edges\n  (:173) looks up only the CHILD symbol, so a parent test needs the parent looked up there too.\n- Commits touching type_hierarchy.py since 08-01: 615471e2e7, 78dd52c779 (docstrings), 562e5a3b8b\n  (derived_from/depends_on), ea22d7023c, 973f673723 -- none changes the gate.\n- Repro: parity CASES[\"cpp\"] -> class Shape modifiers=['abstract'], Shape::area ['virtual','abstract'],\n  Square::area [], extends Square -> Shape, no dispatches_to. Holds.\n- C# abstract-base fixture (abstract class Shape { public abstract int Area(); } / class Square : Shape\n  { public override int Area() ... }) -> Shape ['abstract'], Shape.Area ['abstract'], Square.Area\n  ['override'], extends Square -> Shape, no dispatches_to. Confirms the csharp half; C# already records\n  per-method override.\n- cpp non-pure virtual (virtual int f(){...}) -> Base::f modifiers [] : \"virtual\" is recorded only on\n  pure virtuals, as the item says.\n- tests/test_interface_dispatch_parity.py:111 KNOWN_HOLES[\"cpp\"] still names this cause.\nNot checked: go (struct embedding) and rust behaviour under a widened predicate."  # 5f5e
